+---
+
+## Furry Companion extensions (FCS patch v0.7.1)
+
+The following methods are **not part of the unmodified upstream API**. They are added by the Furry Companion patch bundle. They expose selected Plastic mesh controls from the existing C++ engine; they do not implement a second deformer.
+
+### Scene.buildMeshAdvanced
+
+```javascript
+var meshLevel = scene.buildMeshAdvanced(
+    rasterImage,
+    "mesh_name",
+    targetEdgeLength,   // 2..256 pixels
+    margin,             // 0..128 pixels
+    maxVertices          // 0 means use the builder's default/unbounded target
+);
+```
+
+This is an overload-like additional method; the original `scene.buildMesh(image, name)` remains available and retains its defaults (`15` px edge length, margin `5`, no target vertex cap). The advanced method validates the arguments before calling the same native `MeshBuilder` used by Plastic.
+
+### Level.getMeshInfo / getMeshVertices
+
+```javascript
+var info = meshLevel.getMeshInfo(1);
+// { meshCount, meshes: [{index, vertexCount}, ...], coordinateSpace }
+
+var vertices = meshLevel.getMeshVertices(0, 1);
+// [{index, x, y, rigidity}, ...]
+```
+
+Coordinates are in centered mesh/stage space: origin at image center, positive X to the right, positive Y upward. `rigidity` is the native `RigidPoint.rigidity` value. The methods inspect the actual `TMeshImage`, not a Python approximation.
+
+### Level.setMeshRigidityAtPoint
+
+```javascript
+var changed = meshLevel.setMeshRigidityAtPoint(
+    meshIndex, frame, x, y, radius, rigidity
+);
+```
+
+This paints existing vertices inside a circular radius, then invalidates the native Plastic mesh cache. Valid rigidity range is `1..10000`; the familiar Plastic UI uses `1` for flexible and `10000` for rigid. The return value is the number of vertices changed, allowing the caller to detect a misplaced zone.
+
+### PlasticRig.setVertexAngleLimits
+
+```javascript
+rig.setVertexAngleLimits(vertexIndex, minDegrees, maxDegrees);
+```
+
+Sets the native skeleton vertex's minimum/maximum accepted angle deltas (degrees) and invalidates its compiled Plastic data. This allows Furry Companion to keep joints within an editable angular range. Values must be finite, increasing, and within `[-360, 360]`.
+
+### Compatibility and error behavior
+
+The capability probe in Furry Animation Studio deliberately rejects an unpatched `toonz_headless` binary rather than silently falling back to the old Python deformation engine. `buildMeshAdvanced`, the three mesh inspection/rigidity methods, and `setVertexAngleLimits` must all be present for the FCS native export path.
